\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Tell me the stories of Jesus
\par I love to hear;
\par Things I would ask Him to tell me
\par If He were here:
\par Scence by the wayside,
\par Tales of the sea,
\par Stories of Jesus,
\par Tell them to me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. First let me hear how the children
\par Stood round His knee;
\par And I shall fancy His blessing
\par Resting on me:
\par Words full of kindness,
\par Deeds full of grace,
\par All in the love-light
\par Of Jesu's face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Tell how the sparrow that twitters
\par On yonder tree
\par And the sweet meadow-side lily
\par May speak to me;
\par Give me their message,
\par For I would hear
\par How Jesus taught us
\par Our Father's care.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Tell me, in accents of wonder,
\par How rolled the sea,
\par Tossing the boat in a tempest
\par On Galilee;
\par And how the Master,
\par Ready and kind,
\par Chided the billows
\par And hushed the wind.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Into the city I'd follow
\par The children's band,
\par Waving a branch of the palm-tree
\par High in my hand;
\par One of His heralds,
\par Yes, I would sing
\par Loudest hossanas!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Show me that scene, in the Garden,
\par Of bitter pain;
\par And of the Cross where my Saviour
\par For me was slain:
\par Sad ones or bright ones,
\par So that they be,
\par Stories of Jesus,
\par Tell them to me.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

